 other one old  and one young the twin who went to space  has essentially traveled 40 years ahead  in time the only problem with this is  that you must be traveling near the  speed of light to make any effect and  the fastest human spaceship travels at  only a tiny fraction of the speed to get  near the speed of light we would need to  harness the energy of a star another  theory of time travel was proposed by  physicist  Ranma lat he claims to have figured out  how to make a machine that uses a  circulating beam of light to twist space  and because space and time are connected  his machine to us time this is a model  of his machine real machine will be  about the width of a human hair and with  about 10,000 lasers the lasers work  together to twist the space-time  although this machine won't be able to  think humans back in time they're  planning to use it to thin tiny  particles or information back in time  imagine being able to use it in the  future to send back the cure for AIDS or  cancer the idea of time travel creates  many paradoxes one famous one is the  grandfather's paradox but if you were to  go back in time and kill your  grandfather how could you have ever been  born to go back in time and kill them  many mathematicians believe that the  answer to this is that there are an  infinite number of parallel universes  and every time you make a decision you  create a new universe that was the same  up until the point you made that  decision so if you were to go back in  time and kill your grandfather you would  just create another universe without you  in its future may  in outer space aliens have perfected  time travel or maybe our descendants  have harnessed the energy of a star so  someone knocks on the door claiming to  be your great-great-great great-great  grandchild don't slam the door because  maybe you're descended a thousand years  into the future  got into a time machine to visit their  ancestor
 

